global section — settings for the HAProxy process itself
chroot  - chroot changes the starting point (/) of a process so that it sees only a specific directory tree instead of the entire filesystem, making that directory appear to be the whole system.
chroot locks the process into that directory as its filesystem root, as a security measure — if HAProxy is ever compromised, it can't see or touch files outside /var/lib/haproxy
chroot /var/lib/haproxy

Run as haproxy user and haproxy group.Each program when the installation is happening linux will create a program user and group ie haproxy user and group, same for postgres, ngnix etc.When root start the haproxy then ha proxy run as haproxxy user by below config. Why start as haproxy as root so it can bind 80 and 443 port.But all traffic are contolled as haproxy user.It dosent have complete previlage only previlage to do haproxy operation.
user haproxy
group haproxy

