maxconn 4000 - total simultaneous connections HAProxy will accept
log 127.0.0.1 local0 debug - Enable logging, send to syslog service which is installed in this server ie 127.0.0.1, the purpose of syslog is take the log from all application and store in the file in a place based on the syslog config. local0 is the route that log traverse to syslog ie haproxy log will come from local0 similarly we have local7 till, so for each application we can have own label so syslog identify properly and save to file, debug is writing complete data not filtering anything.local0 is lable and we have some system label as well, like auth, mail etc, those are used for system logs mainly we used this lable is is not to mix all logs together.
pidfile    /var/run/haproxy.pid - Just store the haproxy pid to this file
tune.ssl.default-dh-param    2048 - for ssl encryption use dh method with 2048 bit higher bit number stronger encryption
tune.bufsize 1048576  # Increased from 128KB to 1MB for large SonarQube report uploads - When we send the req from browser to haproxy it will create a temp storage called buffer and save the data, same for resp as well from backend to haproxy to browser. Backend to haproxy data will be stramed ie chunk not full 200mb file
tune.http.maxhdr 200  # Increase the max number of headers - No of http headers allowed.

defaults section — Anything placed inside defaults becomes the default behavior for your frontend, backend, and listen sections unless they override it.
log global - Inherit the same log serting from global to all frontend and backend
option httplog - Give detailed log with path, method, response time, code etc
option forwardfor - for each req send X-Forwarded-For header with client ip to backend
option redispatch - When the haproxy send the req to one backend server and connection lost in middle and retry exhausted, this option will send the same req to other backend server witout failing the req
option http-keep-alive - Keeps the TCP connection between the client and HAProxy open across multiple HTTP requests, instead of opening/closing a new connection per request
When from backend if we are getting 5xx error just return the error message that have in below path 50x.http file for all 500 to 504 error msg.
