errorfile 504 /etc/haproxy/errors/50x.http

listen stats - this is a separate thing entirely from your app traffic it's HAProxy's own built-in monitoring dashboard, a live webpage showing connection counts and backend health, reachable at port 9080 (bind *:9080). Not something you need for traffic analysis, but worth knowing it exists — you can literally open http://<lb-host>:9080/ in a browser right now and see live connection stats while your load test runs.It gives it own health and traffic like backedn status, number of req, connection, uptime, response time etc
listen stats - Here stats can give any name
    bind       *:9080 - * refer if server has many ip it will listent to any ip with port 9080
    mode       http - only via http
    maxconn    10 - 10 simpultenous connection
    stats      enable - Turn the statistic on
    stats      refresh 20s - Refresh sec
    stats      show-legends - Show up down etc
    stats      show-node - Show haproxy name on stat page
    stats      hide-version - hide hapeoxy version
    stats      uri / - if /haproxy then http://ip:9080/haproxy to view stat page else if /then http://ip:9080/
    stats      realm Haproxy\ Statistics
    #stats      auth stats-admin:B1Gp4sSw0rD!!
    option     httplog - Complete http log
    option     logasap - log assoon as possible dont wait for req to complete
    option     dontlognull - ignore log without any data
    timeout    client 100s - Time to wait for connection from browser to haproxy
    timeout    server 100s - Time to wait for response from backend to haproxy
    timeout    connect 100s - backend connection time to connect to backend from haproxy
    timeout    queue 100s - How long req can wait in queue to reach the app server or backend.

