Understanding HAProxy log

-----Start-----
first time - Jul 27 09:15:02 - Added by syslog when it proceess the log 
Second time  - [27/Jul/2026:09:15:02.456] - When haproxy receive the request
0/0/1/45/46 - Tq / Tw / Tc / Tr / Tt 
tq - Total time haproxy wait to accept the request
tw - total wait time for backend to accept the request from haproxy
tc - haproxy to backend tcp connection time
tr - server response time
tt - total time of above

---- - Req end without any issues
--NN - NN mean normal normal ending no issues
--VN - Again end with normal so no issues
Below are the error endings
cD-- - client disconnect, ie bofore sq send resp, client close browser we see this error code
sQ-- - Sqerver issue or time out.
cD → Client disconnected before completion.
sC → Couldn't connect to the backend server.
sH → Server timeout while waiting for headers.
sD → Server closed the connection unexpectedly.
45/45/12/12/0 - actconn / feconn / beconn / srv_conn / retries - 
actconn - Toatl active connection in haproxy
feconn - Toatl active front end connection in haproxy. usually same as actconn, since haproxy has one front end we configured
beconn - total active backend connection
srv_conn - total active connection on particukar one back end server if has many like 2 server in our case
retries - How many retries on that sever for that req
0/0 - server queue/backend queue - server queue means no of req waiting for that server, bckend queue - Total req waiting in queue for both server in case of 2 server we have as backend.
rest other data are like pid and name, client ip,  req path, response code, response size etc all are readable.
