log rotation

-----Start-----
For any program like haproxy, ngnix all the files logs needs to be rotated.elase it will grow and fill the disk size
The logrotation rules will be written here.The rules will be auto crreated when the program installed, else it will be created by admins. Here when it rotate the log it will create a new log empty file with same name and old file it will rename to haproxy.log.1 and 2 day old log ile it will zip and rename to haproxy.2.tz and same till 7th day and last 8 file will be deleted.
/etc/logrotate.d/haproxy
haproxy rules
/var/log/haproxy.log {
    daily - rotate daily
    rotate 7 - keep for 7 day old data, 
    compress - old files it will compress
    missingok - if no log file show no error
    notifempty - donot rotate if file is empty
    create 640 root adm - provide complete access
    postrotate
        systemctl reload rsyslog - after rotate just reload the syslog program
    endscript
}

-----End-----

